<section class="hero"><div class="container hero-grid"><div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-dot"></span> Food systems, clearly explained</p><h1>Food supply under pressure.<br><em>Facts before fear.</em></h1><p class="hero-deck">What is happening to the world's food supply—and what does it mean for prices, farmers and households? We connect the evidence, explain the trade-offs and show what to watch next.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-light" href="#analysis">Explore the analysis <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link text-link-light" href="/data/">Go to the data desk <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><p class="hero-note">A high price, a local shortage and acute hunger are related—but they are not the same thing.</p></div><div class="hero-visual" aria-label="Illustration of the path from harvest to market"><div class="orbit orbit-one"></div><div class="orbit orbit-two"></div><div class="hero-sun"></div><div class="field-lines"></div><div class="grain grain-one"></div><div class="grain grain-two"></div><div class="grain grain-three"></div><div class="hero-stamp"><span>THE FOOD SYSTEM</span><strong>One chain.<br>Many pressure points.</strong><small>Production · Trade · Access</small></div><div class="visual-caption"><span class="visual-dot"></span> Follow evidence from field to table</div></div></div></section>
