<section class="signal-section"><div class="container"><div class="section-kicker">The latest verified picture</div><div class="section-title-row"><div><h2>Three numbers. Three different stories.</h2><p class="section-intro">Current indicators matter—but each measures something different.</p></div><a class="arrow-link" href="/data/">See sources and context <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
<div class="metric-grid">
<article class="metric-card metric-warm"><div class="metric-top"><span class="metric-label">Global food commodity prices</span><span class="metric-icon" aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div><p class="metric-number">136.0 <span>points</span></p><p class="metric-detail"><strong>Highest since November 2022;</strong> +1.5% month on month and +5.8% year on year in September.</p><div class="metric-foot">FAO Food Price Index · 2 Oct 2026</div><a href="/articles/food-prices-vs-shortages/">What the index does—and doesn't—say <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article>
<article class="metric-card metric-green"><div class="metric-top"><span class="metric-label">Global cereal production forecast</span><span class="metric-icon" aria-hidden="true">⌁</span></div><p class="metric-number">2.979 <span>billion tonnes</span></p><p class="metric-detail">Forecast for 2026: 2.1% below the 2025 record, but still the <strong>second-largest harvest on record</strong>.</p><div class="metric-foot">FAO Cereal Brief · 2 Oct 2026</div><a href="/articles/global-cereal-outlook-2026/">Read the global cereal outlook <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article>
<article class="metric-card metric-blue"><div class="metric-top"><span class="metric-label">People facing acute food insecurity</span><span class="metric-icon" aria-hidden="true">◎</span></div><p class="metric-number">266 <span>million</span></p><p class="metric-detail">People across 47 food-crisis countries and territories experienced high levels of acute food insecurity in 2025.</p><div class="metric-foot">Global Report on Food Crises 2026</div><a href="/articles/food-security-vs-availability/">Why hunger can coexist with supply <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article>
</div><p class="small-print">These figures are not directly interchangeable: one is an international commodity-price index, one is a production forecast, and one measures acute food insecurity in analyzed crisis settings. <a href="/data/">Sources and definitions</a>.</p></div></section>
